An interrupt from user mode, for the host to take on its tick: WebAssembly has no asynchronous
trap, so a task enters the kernel only through syscalls, and a loop that makes none kept its cpu
for good and never saw a signal, not even SIGKILL. The `user_interrupt` export does what an
interrupt from user mode does elsewhere (expired timers and the scheduler tick, signals, a
reschedule if wanted), between two instructions of the program; the engine calls it from
wasmtime's epoch callback (engine/src/user.rs on_epoch).

diff --git a/arch/wasm/kernel/syscall.c b/arch/wasm/kernel/syscall.c
index 6de7190ce4a5..f4e3d5b4864b 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/arch/wasm/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -70,6 +70,39 @@ wasm_syscall(long nr, unsigned long arg0, unsigned long arg1,
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * An interrupt taken in user mode. WebAssembly has no asynchronous trap, so a task otherwise
+ * enters the kernel only through syscalls, and a loop that makes none keeps its cpu for good
+ * and never sees a signal, not even SIGKILL. The host calls this from between two instructions
+ * of such a program, on its periodic tick: what an interrupt from user mode does elsewhere.
+ * Expired timers fire (the scheduler tick with them), a pending signal is delivered (a fatal
+ * one ends the task here, and this never returns), and the task gives up its cpu if the
+ * scheduler wants it. The program is in no syscall: its pt_regs, which a signal handler's
+ * nested syscalls also use, are as they were afterwards.
+ */
+__attribute__((export_name("user_interrupt"))) void wasm_user_interrupt(void)
+{
+	struct pt_regs *regs = current_pt_regs();
+	struct pt_regs saved = *regs;
+
+	local_irq_disable();
+	rcu_note_context_switch(false);
+	regs->user_mode = 0;
+	regs->syscall_nr = -1;
+	regs->syscall_return = 0;
+	regs->restart_syscall_nr = -1;
+	irqentry_enter_from_user_mode(regs);
+
+	wasm_timer_check();
+	wasm_service_remote_request(current);
+	/* run what that made pending: the timer interrupt itself */
+	local_irq_enable();
+	local_irq_disable();
+
+	irqentry_exit_to_user_mode(regs);
+	*regs = saved;
+}
+
